# Documentation PR and merge workflow

For every repository documentation change—including `docs/**`, `AGENTS.md`,
`CLAUDE.md`, `README*`, `CONTRIBUTING*`, and `.cursor/rules/**`:

1. Start from the current `origin/main` in a dedicated branch/worktree.
2. Make the smallest authoritative change and preserve historical entries.
3. Run relevant documentation checks (`check:kb-links`, document-size,
   `git diff --check`, and any document-specific verifier).
4. Commit the change, open a concise PR, and merge it through GitHub after the
   required checks pass. Never edit or merge directly on `main`.
5. Report the merged PR, verification results, and intentionally unchanged docs.

This workflow does not authorize production, schema, RLS, security, migration,
cron, or operational changes. Keep their separate approval and audit gates.
If another agent owns the same document, coordinate rather than overwrite it.
Honor an explicit user request to hold, draft, or not merge.
